        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C12521</IRI>
        <Literal>A blood cell specialized for oxygen transport, having a high concentration of hemoglobin in the cytoplasm. They are biconcave, anucleate discs, with a 6-8um diameter in humans. [Definition Source: NCIT]</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
