        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C20674</IRI>
        <Literal>A human early embryonic event in which in any given cell one of a female&apos;s two X chromosomes becomes inactivated and converted into a Barr body.  After inactivation has occurred, all descendants of that cell have the same inactivated X chromosome. Thus, X-inactivation creates cell clones with differing effective gene content. An organism whose cells vary in effective gene content and hence in the expression of a trait, is called a genetic mosaic. [Definition Source: NCIT]</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
