        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C3389</IRI>
        <Literal>An anxiety disorder precipitated by an experience of intense fear or horror while exposed to a traumatic (especially life-threatening) event. The disorder is characterized by intrusive recurring thoughts or images of the traumatic event; avoidance of anything associated with the event; a state of hyperarousal and diminished emotional responsiveness. These symptoms are present for at least one month and the disorder is usually long-term. [Definition Source: NCIT]</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
