        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C44459</IRI>
        <Literal>A synthetic, light sensitive, volatile, colorless, liquid that is miscible with many non-polar organic solvents. Trichloroethylene is used mainly as a degreaser for metal parts. Upon combustion, it produces irritants and toxic gases. Occupational exposure to trichloroethylene is associated with excess incidences of liver cancer, kidney cancer and non-Hodgkin lymphoma. It is reasonably anticipated to be a human carcinogen. (NCI05) [Definition Source: NCIT]</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
