        <IRI>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C92621</IRI>
        <Literal>An anxiety disorder precipitated by an experience of intense fear or horror while exposed to a traumatic (especially life-threatening) event. The disorder is characterized by dissociative symptoms; vivid recollections of the traumatic event; avoidance of stimuli associated with the traumatic event; and a constant state of hyperarousal for no more than one month. [Definition Source: NCIT]</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
