        <Literal>Short-chain fatty acid producing bacteria are a type of gut microbiota that convert non-digestible carbohydrates into short-chain fatty acids, primarily acetate, propionate, and butyrate, which play a crucial role in maintaining gut health and immune function. [Definition Source: llama3-8b-8192]</Literal>
